@page "/"

@* Landing page for the LumaCore Web UI preview.
   Gives a short overview of what this UI is and where it is heading. *@

<h1>Welcome to the LumaCore UI (Preview)</h1>

<p>
	This is an early preview of the LumaCore Web UI.
	It is intentionally minimal: a small, self-hosted shell that will grow together
	with the orchestrator and the personas that live inside it.
</p>

<section class="lc-section">
	@* High-level expectations for what this UI will eventually offer *@
	<h2>What you can expect here</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Basic status views for your LumaCore instance</li>
		<li>Simple controls to trigger test generations</li>
		<li>A home for your personas: overview, details, memory, and more</li>
		<li>Configuration and tooling focused on clarity, self-hosting, and control</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="lc-section">
	@* Short explanation of how the UI connects to the backend orchestrator *@
	<h2>Backend connection</h2>
	<p>
		The UI is designed to talk to a running LumaCore orchestrator instance.
		In the next steps, we will:
	</p>
	<ol>
		<li>Configure the backend base URL</li>
		<li>Add a small health/status call</li>
		<li>Wire in JWT authentication for protected endpoints</li>
	</ol>
	<p>
		You can already visit the <NavLink href="status" class="...">Status</NavLink> page to see a live health check
		once your backend is reachable.
	</p>
</section>
